-- title:
--   A location-sensitive bound for the first Type I tail block
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge4$, $(a,q)=1$, $|\beta|\le q^{-2}$, and $C,B\ge0$. For the specified first odd tail block, the capped reciprocal-sine sum along the perturbed rational grid is at most
--   $$\frac Cq+B\left(\frac{2q}{\pi}\log(4q)+4q\right).$$
--   The cap at an odd divisor $d$ is $C/d+B$. The first-block locations allow the varying cap to be charged only once at size $C/q$.
-- source:
--   Terence Tao, Every odd number greater than 1 is the sum of at most five primes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6656, Sections 5 and 6. Original Lean source: Theorems/Thm_TaoFivePrimes_vaughan_typeI_first_tail_location_sensitive.lean, lines 701-883.

